From ef5c774e72769fd6f6696827f534955fc04aefbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luannt <luannt.devops@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:22:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cmd,ui,app): resuming a session no longer rewrites the
 project's model

`run -s/-C` through the server and opening a session in the TUI restored that
session's last model by writing it to the project's .crush/crush.json, so every
later session silently moved to it (and the write replaced the whole models
entry, dropping effort/think settings). In local mode the restore switched the
model in memory only, so the same command ran different providers depending on
the mode. Resuming now runs the workspace's current model and writes nothing;
when it differs from the session's last model one line says so (stderr for the
CLI, status bar in the TUI with an alt+p or alt+m hint). Explicit choices still
write: -m, --small-model, --reasoning-effort, alt+p/alt+m, thinking/effort,
agent-cli-tmux new --model. scripts/eval/session-model.sh checks both modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
